The function also includes test cases to verify that the output list contains unique prime numbers and that their sum is divisible by 10.

Please note that due to the nature of the problem, it may take a long time to find a valid set of prime numbers that meet all the conditions.

Also, the function `math.isqrt(n)` is used to get the integer square root of a number. This function is available in Python 3.8 and later. If you are using an earlier version of Python, you can replace `math.isqrt(n)` with `int(math.sqrt(n))`.

